GITHUB pages version 

• The quickest route is Quarto’s built-in GitHub Pages publisher. Your site should appear at:

  https://trevorhastie.github.io/ESL-Website/

  From Terminal:

  cd ~/GITHUB/ESL-Website
  git push origin main
  quarto publish gh-pages

  When Quarto asks whether to publish, answer Y. It will render the site, create a gh-pages branch, and push the generated HTML.  _site/ remains excluded from the main branch. This is Quarto’s recommended simple publishing method. Quarto GitHub Pages guide  (https://quarto.org/docs/publishing/github-pages.html)

  Then:

  1. Visit github.com/trevorhastie/ESL-Website (https://github.com/trevorhastie/ESL-Website).
  2. Select Settings → Pages.
  3. Under Build and deployment, confirm:
      - Source: Deploy from a branch
      - Branch: gh-pages
      - Folder: /(root)

  4. Click Save if needed.
  5. Visit:

  https://trevorhastie.github.io/ESL-Website/

  The first publication can take up to ten minutes. You can monitor it under the repository’s Actions tab. GitHub Pages
  publishing documentation
  (https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/configuring-a-publishing-source-for-your-github-pages-site)

  For later updates, commit your work and run:

  git push origin main
  quarto publish gh-pages

  This publishes a public preview only; it does not affect hastie.su.domains.



